## Pedagogical Progression & Dependencies

1. **Cluster Bootstrapping & Foundations (00–02)**: Initialize Kubernetes from bare nodes using `kubeadm` (Standard or
   HA), establish CLI speed with `jsonpath`, and deploy monitoring addons via `helm`.
1. **Identity & Core Primitives (03–06)**: Secure cluster access with `rbac` before launching atomic `pods`, then
   decouple application state via `configmaps` and `secrets`.
1. **Workload Management (07–09)**: Scale and roll out workloads via `deployments`, manage background tasks with
   `workloads-advanced`, and manage multi-environment overlays with `kustomize`.
1. **Pod Placement & Routing (10–11)**: Constrain pod scheduling across cluster nodes via `scheduling`, and configure
   service discovery, ingress, and microsegmentation via `networking`.
1. **Storage & State (12–13)**: Master static volume bindings and reclaim policies in `volumes`, then advance to dynamic
   CSI provisioners and delayed binding in `storage-classes`.
1. **Cluster Administration & Capstone (14–19)**: Extend APIs with `crds-operators`,
   safeguard cluster state with `etcd`, perform maintenance with `upgrade`, diagnose real-world
   multi-fault failures in `cluster-troubleshooting`, and manage resilient multi-master topology
   and rolling upgrades in `ha-cluster`.

